                <pb facs="0203" n="993" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v01p2/pg993"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>At the Washington Tripartite Foreign Ministers Meeting of July 10–14, 1953,
                    Secretary Dulles, British Acting Foreign Secretary Salisbury, and French Foreign
                    Minister Bidault agreed that, in the event of an armistice in Korea, the trade
                    embargo against the People’s Republic of Ghina would be continued. For
                    documentation <pb facs="0204" n="994" xml:id="pg994"/> concerning this
                    agreement, see <ref target="frus:frus1952-54v14p1">volume XIV</ref>. Concerning
                    the Korean armistice, which was signed on July 27, 1953, see <ref
                        target="frus:frus1952-54v15p1">volume XV</ref>. The major portion of
                    documentation on the Washington Tripartite Foreign Ministers Meeting, is printed
                    in <ref target="frus:frus1952-54v05p2/pg_1582">volume V, Part 2, pages
                        1582</ref> ff.</p>
            </div>
